  "notes": "A formal, written-style word. In everyday conversation, {似|に}ている or {似|に}たような are more natural.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {類似|るいじ}{品|ひん} (imitation product, knockoff)\n- {類似|るいじ}{点|てん} (point of similarity)\n- {類似|るいじ}{性|せい} (similarity — as a measurable property)\n- ～に{類似|るいじ}する (to resemble ~)\n- {類似|るいじ}した{事例|じれい} (similar cases)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {類似|るいじ} is formal and analytical\n- {似|に}ている is the everyday equivalent\n- {酷似|こくじ} means striking resemblance (stronger)",
